WEBVTT

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.620
Fresh meat is the best meat!

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:12.140
I'd love to try plant-based food before I die!

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:14.370
How extravagant!

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:19.320
Anyway, the Worms were
 awfully irritated today.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:20.370
Hm?

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:28.360
What's with that guy?

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.300
He's in a suit in the middle of the desert!

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.550
He's not long for this world.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:35.760
No kidding! He's carrying his own tombstone!

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:27.410
<i>It's been three days since 
the tragedy in Jeneora Rock.</i>

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:33.270
<i>The chain of incidents has been linked 
to the wanted criminal Vash the Stampede.</i>

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:30.690
I can't believe he's sleeping so soundly.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:38.970
<i>Additionally, a man and a woman have 
been identified as possible accomplices.</i>

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:44.790
<i>The seven cities' military police are also 
searching for them as persons of interest.</i>

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.930
So now we're wanted, too?

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:49.580
If headquarters finds out, we'll be fired.

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.510
<i>And now, the weather for the seven cities...</i>

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.350
It's his. He doesn't want it.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:02.590
What? But yesterday...

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:06.230
He hasn't eaten. Not since that day.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:13.330
Only god really knows 
what goes on inside someone.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:23.760
A sandstorm?

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:25.600
No, those are...

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.850
Worms.

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:32.620
In these parts, they're
 an important source of protein.

00:03:32.620 --> 00:03:35.970
If you can stomach the way 
they look, they're not bad.

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:39.050
I think stomaching <i>that</i>
 would be the hard part.

00:03:53.510 --> 00:03:54.580
Are you all right?!

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.060
You're not dying on me!

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.020
Excuse me! This man is hurt...

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:34.210
It's too late for these folks.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:37.150
They came all the way out here?

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:39.440
"They"?

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.380
Okay...

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.980
O father in heaven,

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.180
forgive us our sins
 as we forgive our neighbors.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:29.490
May you accept our fallen brethren

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:33.020
and welcome the departed to your...

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.620
What is it?

00:05:35.620 --> 00:05:39.300
Welcome them to your... dinner?

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.110
No, that's a meal.

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:44.320
Deliver them unto your... design?

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.490
No, nobody's talking about fashion.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.880
Uh, give us a drive...

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:55.170
He's not your chauffeur, you idiot.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:57.870
Are you really a priest?

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:01.110
I'm no priest. Just an undertaker.

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:03.800
Now back off. You're ruining it.

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:09.050
Anyway, what's this cross? It's way too huge.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:11.800
Hey, keep your mitts off of it.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.050
What?

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:14.790
Hey, you two.

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.450
Here.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.000
You're hungry, right?

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:31.370
It's good.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.890
Maybe you should leave him be—

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:37.850
I lost my parents, too. 
I grew up in an orphanage.

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:41.720
Good, right?

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:47.460
No matter how heavy a cross you carry,

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:50.050
you still deserve to eat. 
You still deserve to laugh.

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:07.270
Twenty thousand?!

00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:08.620
What a rip-off!

00:07:08.620 --> 00:07:11.700
You should've asked my rates 
before asking me to work, dolts.

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:14.990
You volunteered yourself 
before we even could!

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.210
Did not.

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:17.660
You can't talk your way out of this!

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:19.540
Man, you're dogged.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:19.540
Are we done?

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:22.420
I won't brook this injustice!

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:24.710
Wait, what's this ridiculous price?

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:26.520
What? Stop blabbering and pay up!

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:31.770
By the way, aren't you hurt? 
You got hit by a car, but you look fine.

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:35.050
Yeah, I'm tough. It's my saving grace.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:42.230
An earthquake?

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:43.720
No, this is...

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:02.920
A Grand Worm!

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:32.860
No way!

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:43.230
Are you okay?

00:08:43.230 --> 00:08:45.000
Yes, thank you.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.350
Ew, it's so damp.

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:58.320
Watch your step.

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:06.230
Come on!

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:09.520
Wait, take a look.

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:14.460
They're resonating?

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:19.580
So it's true. 
The Worms really are interconnected.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:22.050
That's their detached electron network.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:26.770
The bigger the Worm, 
the more detached electrons it holds.

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:31.090
This guy must be the pillar 
of the Worms in the area.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:32.390
Meaning?

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:35.080
He's the boss around here.

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:36.720
Oh, hey!

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:45.180
Wait!

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.440
Which hole did he go into?

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.630
I envy kids and their light feet.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:00.620
Why don't you put down that cross, then?

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:05.580
It's the tool of my trade. How would 
I make a living if I offloaded it?

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:10.420
We need to hurry.

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:11.830
Then we should split up.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:13.650
Needle-noggin, you take the farthest one.

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:14.370
"Needle-noggin"?

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:16.300
Little missy can take the next one.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:17.460
My name is Meryl Stryfe!

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:19.420
Uncle Downer can go there.

00:10:19.930 --> 00:10:22.010
And I'll take that one.

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:23.900
Why're <i>you</i> calling the shots?

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:25.660
I thought you were in a hurry.

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:31.440
I don't get it.

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:35.660
Why split up when there's 
no telling what could happen?

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:47.410
N-No one's there, right?

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:54.380
Are you all right?!

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:01.640
Thank goodness.

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:22.930
No luck. I can't find them anywhere.

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:25.040
Me neither.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:29.590
That's enough. You should find 
a way out unless you wanna die, too.

00:11:29.590 --> 00:11:33.250
I'm sure they're both fine. 
We'll find and help them.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:38.460
So you'd risk your life for theirs?

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:44.560
Self-sacrifice on self-sacrifice...
You're a weird one.

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:55.460
You only get one life.

00:11:56.450 --> 00:12:00.190
You have to fight for it, no matter 
who you hurt in the process.

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:04.020
There's no other way to survive.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:07.870
Watch out, Stampede.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:10.700
They take the first bite
 to get your guard down,

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:13.990
then lace what they pass 
to their target with poison.

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:16.670
Standard stuff for assassins.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:17.470
Huh?

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:20.770
Our news agency isn't much to be proud of,

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:23.510
but one thing we <i>do</i> have 
is a good intel network.

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:28.160
I've heard about humans who control Worms.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:30.020
Who, me?

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:33.920
That makes no sense, you dolt. 
I'm stuck in here with you.

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:39.310
In that case, let me check out 
that precious cross of yours.

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:42.030
This isn't funny anymore.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:47.160
From the look of it, 
it's too heavy to be a mere cross.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:49.510
Give me a peek inside, why don't you?

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:52.750
Why don't you make me?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:56.560
With your derringer that looks
 too light to be a real gun, hmm?

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:58.790
Come on, you two.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:03.190
Stampede, this is a man who can 
kill with a smile on his face.

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:05.740
No, I don't think so.

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:07.260
Why's that?

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:11.260
I can see it in his eyes.

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:19.060
You really mess with me.

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:21.440
See?

00:13:25.310 --> 00:13:26.570
Roberto?

00:13:30.390 --> 00:13:32.010
Meryl!

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:36.250
Roberto!

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:39.670
It's pointless. They've all been digested.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:45.330
This place is covered in skeletons,
so the Worms can't digest <i>that</i> much.

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:47.660
Besides, I haven't seen 
a single one of their bones.

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:49.510
What about it?

00:13:49.510 --> 00:13:52.110
It's too early to give up.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:58.520
So, how long do you want 
to keep wandering in circles?

00:13:59.590 --> 00:14:00.930
Um...

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:05.910
Maybe we're the lost ones, not them.

00:14:05.910 --> 00:14:09.280
Come on... Stop trying to scare me.

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:26.610
So we were in its nose...

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:29.060
Hey, you guys! Are you all right?!

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:30.760
It's a Worm spout!

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:33.390
I've never seen such a big one before!

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.830
Run! Hurry! Behind you!

00:14:35.830 --> 00:14:38.940
Beat it! Hurry! Run! Come on!

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:43.460
Hey, <i>hey!</i> You just lucked out and 
you're gonna throw it all away?

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:49.510
There's no guarantee you'll get lucky again!

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:51.030
You should run.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:52.480
Don't do it!

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:53.560
You'll die!

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:55.240
Run! Hurry!

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:56.660
You fool...

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:24.800
You're...

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:32.660
You're all right now.

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:38.660
A little too careless, aren't we?

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:44.820
We only met today. How many times 
have you let me out of your sight?

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:49.220
Yet not once did you shoot me.

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:54.920
That unique mosquito sound...

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:59.870
So you're the one controlling the Worms.

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:05.190
That's odd. It should be 
inaudible to regular humans.

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:07.980
Good job seeing through my disguise.

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:10.330
Did you kill that couple, too?

00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:13.300
Humans always assume it's a family

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:15.820
when they see a group of adults and children.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:18.580
Where are Meryl and Roberto?

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:21.370
You came back for them?

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:27.770
I simply don't understand...

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:33.220
Didn't you realize returning
for them would get you killed?

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:44.460
Give them back!

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:48.420
If you must know what happened 
to them, then make me talk.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:52.430
Damn it...

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:55.700
You're leaving yourself wide open again.

00:17:04.810 --> 00:17:06.290
Eat this.

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:12.850
Pathetic Worm!

00:17:34.410 --> 00:17:35.870
Who are you?

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:38.280
Just an undertaker.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:41.860
I'll be seeing you.

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:46.420
That is... assuming you get out of here alive.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.040
Hey, wait!

00:17:56.230 --> 00:18:00.210
You're got getting away, Worm.

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:09.080
I'm a tough nut to crack.

00:18:36.160 --> 00:18:38.460
Fresh meat is definitely the best!

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:41.290
What, you still feeling sick?

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:43.640
No, I'm fine thanks to you...

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:48.840
I appreciate you saving me—

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:48.840
Here, eat.

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:50.380
I'm fine...

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:52.970
You're not going so survive like that.

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:55.150
Come on! Eat up!

00:18:55.970 --> 00:18:58.750
Hey! What do you think you're doing?!

00:18:56.940 --> 00:19:01.460
I see now. The cross is 
actually a machine gun.

00:19:01.460 --> 00:19:03.510
No wonder it's so heavy.

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:08.500
I told you he's bad news.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.170
But we made it through thanks to him.

00:19:11.170 --> 00:19:15.090
You'd thank a villain for his vagaries?

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:17.430
That's a little too generous.

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:20.470
I get that a lot.

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:26.100
Then fix it already...

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.780
Just eat up already.

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:31.960
I told you, I'm fine.

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:33.820
Don't be picky with your food.

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:35.340
That's not the deal.

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:36.540
Then what is?

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:42.220
Vash...

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:47.290
I still deserve to eat and laugh, right?

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:52.350
The name's Nicholas D. Wolfwood.

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:55.050
Vash the Stampede—

00:19:55.050 --> 00:19:56.090
Needle-noggin.

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:57.360
N-Needle-noggin?

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:00.950
Welp, let's get going.

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:02.970
Wait, you're coming with us?

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:04.510
You need someone like me, don't you?

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:06.970
Seems you're dealing 
with some unsavory types.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.120
Thank you, but no.

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:09.660
I won't be too expensive.

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:11.270
No, thanks.

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:14.000
You should be asking why 
he thinks he can charge us.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:15.980
Please say something, Roberto!

00:20:15.980 --> 00:20:20.480
Well, we're just tagging along 
without permission, too.

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:22.310
It's totally different!

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:26.070
Huh, I didn't expect him 
to be the reasonable one.

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:27.910
Gimme one.

00:20:28.300 --> 00:20:30.180
I didn't say you could have one.

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:31.940
Don't be so cheap.

00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:34.480
No! We can't afford any more expenditure!

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:36.170
Look! Check out the sky.

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:37.860
What now? This is important...

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:44.170
How pretty.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:50.040
Those are all Worms.

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:52.280
Thanks for ruining it.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:06.570
You overdid it. 
You almost got me killed, too...

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:11.130
Zazie the Beast.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:15.000
But you earned their trust, right?

00:21:15.840 --> 00:21:19.620
Besides, killing "friends" is your favorite.

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:25.240
You honestly couldn't care less 
about human lives, could you?

00:21:27.650 --> 00:21:29.650
I can see it in your eyes.

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:32.360
Hah, I don't care.

00:21:32.810 --> 00:21:35.270
I just do my job,

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:38.160
no matter who I'm up against.

00:21:42.520 --> 00:21:47.470
What Vash the Stampede 
manifested at that moment

00:21:47.470 --> 00:21:50.310
must be the gate that allows access 
to the higher dimension.

00:21:50.980 --> 00:21:54.420
But it's still locked.

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:57.790
His morality and ethics are 
functioning as a defensive measure.

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:04.500
Your little brother is
 more human than anyone.

00:22:09.840 --> 00:22:13.150
Then we'll just have to pry it open.

00:22:15.250 --> 00:22:18.640
We'll destroy him if we have to.
